From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] D18 item 1: the almanac-HDOP scorer, built from public
 material as Kshana's own method (not a reproduction of the cited paper)

src/interference_map/almanac_hdop.rs: a YUMA almanac reader (the 10-bit week resolved
near a stated week), the IS-GPS-200 almanac orbit, HDOP at a geodetic position with a
stated elevation mask, the NACp 95 % bound (nacp_epu_bound_m, quoted from the open
textbook The 1090 Megahertz Riddle, Table 1.9), and the flag EPU > multiple * 2 * HDOP *
UERE, with the mask, UERE and multiple stated by the caller (no defaults).

Acceptance (tests/almanac_hdop.rs and the module tests): HDOP equals the numpy oracle at
the 20 points to 1.6e-15 with the same satellite counts (limit 1e-9); the NACp mapping
equals the quoted table; the flag is exact on the 12 hand-written reports.
docs/observatory/METHOD.md says what was built, from which public sources, and that it
does not reproduce the paper; the observatory does not use it, and scoring real data is
its own pre-registration. Catalogue messages and an allowance for the YUMA field names.
